  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 14 October 2026</p>
</header>
<p>This policy explains what information Yong Social Finance uses, why, and the choices you have. It is written to match how the app works.</p>
<h2>1. Who we are</h2><p>Yong Social Finance (the "app", "we", "us") is operated by YongSocialCo. The app gives you market prices, news, videos and tools for learning about money, investing and digital assets. It is available at app.yongsocial.com and as an Android app.</p><p>For privacy questions, contact us at <a href="mailto:yongsocial@outlook.com">yongsocial@outlook.com</a>.</p><h2>2. The short version</h2><ul><li>You don't need an account, and we don't ask for your name, phone number or payment details.</li><li>Most of what the app remembers (bookmarks, your watchlist and country choice) stays on your phone.</li><li>We don't sell your personal information.</li><li>Some services we use, such as Google, collect technical data. Their own privacy policies apply to them.</li></ul><h2>3. Information stored on your device</h2><p>The app saves some information in your browser's local storage on your phone. This includes:</p><ul><li>your bookmarked articles and your watchlist of coins and stocks;</li><li>the country you chose, or the one the app detected;</li><li>recently downloaded prices and articles, kept so the app loads faster and works when your connection is weak.</li></ul><p>This information is not sent to us. It stays on your device until you clear the app's data or uninstall the app.</p><p>We detect your likely country from your phone's time zone and language settings. This happens on your device, and we don't send it to us. You can change it at any time in the Profile tab.</p><h2>4. Information we receive</h2><ul><li><strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you write, and we use it only to reply and handle your request.</li><li><strong>Technical data from the services the app uses.</strong> When the app loads content or you open a link, the service you connect to may receive your IP address, device and browser type, the pages you visit, and approximate location based on your IP address. Section 5 lists these services.</li><li><strong>Aggregated usage information.</strong> We may look at overall figures, such as how many people opened a section, that don't identify you.</li></ul><p>We don't collect precise GPS location, contacts, photos or microphone data.</p><h2>5. Third-party services</h2><p>The app uses or links to the following services. Each handles data under its own privacy policy, and we don't control them. Please read their policies.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>What it's used for</th><th>Data it may receive</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Google (Blogger, YouTube, Google Play)</td><td>Articles, embedded videos and the Play listing</td><td>Technical data such as IP address and device information; cookies set by YouTube and Google</td></tr><tr><td>CoinGecko</td><td>Crypto prices and exchange prices</td><td>IP address and request details, from the phone making the request</td></tr><tr><td>Alternative.me</td><td>Fear &amp; Greed Index</td><td>IP address and request details</td></tr><tr><td>TradingView</td><td>Stock quotes and charts on the Stocks tab</td><td>IP address, device and browser information; cookies set by TradingView</td></tr><tr><td>Partner trading platforms (for example Roqqu, Grow and Will Trade)</td><td>When you tap "Open" or a referral link</td><td>Once you leave the app, their site handles your data. Referral links may set cookies to track sign-ups.</td></tr><tr><td>X, Telegram, WhatsApp</td><td>Follow links on our social channels</td><td>Handled by each platform when you open it</td></tr></tbody></table><p>When you tap a partner link, the partner may pay us a commission if you sign up, at no extra cost to you. We don't receive your personal details from them through the app.</p><h2>6. Advertising</h2><p>The app doesn't use third-party advertising networks, and we don't share your information with advertisers. Advertisements shown in the app are placed directly by us. Any website an advertisement links to has its own privacy policy.</p><h2>7. How we use information</h2><ul><li>to run the app, show prices and news, and remember your bookmarks, watchlist and country;</li><li>to keep the app working, fast and secure, and to fix problems;</li><li>to reply to your messages;</li><li>to understand, in aggregate, which features people use;</li><li>to comply with the law and protect our users and the app.</li></ul><h2>8. Sharing</h2><p>We don't sell your personal information. We share information only with:</p><ul><li>the service providers listed in section 5, to the extent needed for them to work;</li><li>authorities, when the law requires it or to protect people's rights and safety.</li></ul><h2>9. Cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>The app itself uses local storage, described in section 3. Services we connect to, such as YouTube, Google and TradingView, may set their own cookies. You can control cookies in your browser or phone settings, and clearing the app's data removes the local storage.</p><h2>10. Children</h2><p>The app is intended for adults. It's not directed at children under 18, and we don't knowingly collect their personal information. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we'll delete it.</p><h2>11. Financial content</h2><p>Nothing in the app is financial advice. Information about investing, prices and platforms is for general information only. Please read our <a href="https://app.yongsocial.com/terms-of-use">Terms of Use</a>.</p><h2>12. Security</h2><p>We take reasonable steps to protect information, including using secure connections (HTTPS) for the app and the services it connects to. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we can't guarantee absolute security.</p><h2>13. How long we keep information</h2><ul><li>On your device: until you clear the app's data or uninstall the app.</li><li>Emails you send us: as long as needed to reply and keep records required by law, then deleted.</li></ul><h2>14. Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can:</p><ul><li>change your country at any time in the Profile tab;</li><li>remove bookmarks and your watchlist, or clear all app data, in your phone's settings (Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Yong Social &gt; Storage &gt; Clear data);</li><li>uninstall the app to remove everything stored on your device;</li><li>control cookies in your browser or phone settings;</li><li>ask us for a copy of, correction of, or deletion of any personal information we hold, by emailing <a href="mailto:yongsocial@outlook.com">yongsocial@outlook.com</a>.</li></ul><p>Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under local data protection laws. For users in Nigeria, these include rights under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, and you may complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission. Users in the UK or EU have similar rights under UK GDPR or GDPR. We'll respond to requests within the time the law requires.</p><h2>15. International transfers</h2><p>The services we use are based in different countries, so your information may be processed outside your country. Where required, we rely on the safeguards those services provide.</p><h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. We'll change the "last updated" date at the top of this page. If the changes are significant, we'll tell you in the app.</p><h2>17. Contact us</h2><p>YongSocialCo<br />Email: <a href="mailto:yongsocial@outlook.com">yongsocial@outlook.com</a></p>
